# ── Credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase's Android config. Not a password — it ships inside every APK and
# Google documents it as non-secret — but this repository is PUBLIC and the
# `api_key` inside is billable the moment it is left unrestricted in Google
# Cloud. Partner gets its OWN Android app inside the same Firebase project,
# because a Firebase app is keyed by package name and this one is
# `com.cartze.partner`.
android/app/google-services.json

# The customer app keeps map and geocoding keys in `src/common/secrets.ts`.
# This app has no map — a shop does not move — so the file should stay absent.
# Ignored anyway: the day somebody adds one, it must not be the day it is
# committed.
src/common/secrets.ts
